NEXT

  Finish R1's fix order before P3, one bumped version each, with a
  failing-first test, a sandbox/demo-<version> for Fred where the nested
  window can show it, the record's status lines, and every affected doc
  updated (W19 lists them):

  1. R1 finding 12: new windows split the last leaf, not the focused
     window. on_map puts the new client on top of the focus stack before
     tp_arrange, so sync_tree's "near" (tp_focus_top) is the new window
     itself. It is not in the tree yet, so sync_tree falls back to the
     last leaf (src/client.c on_map, src/layout/arrange.c sync_tree).
     A likely fix: have sync_tree take the most recently focused visible
     window that is already in the tree. Test: in
     tests/test_input_headless.c, focus c0 in [c0 | c1], open a window,
     and check that it splits c0. Expect older tests that assumed
     last-leaf placement to need updating; read each failure before
     changing an expectation. Demo: sandbox/demo-0.1.11, nested; three
     terminals, focus the first, open a fourth, and see where it lands.
     Fixing this also makes the sync_tree comment true.
  2. R1 findings 4 (fullscreen across map and remap) and 5 (xdg popups
     never unconstrained).
  3. R1 findings 9, 11 and 15 to 17: write them into the P3 and P4
